        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Theodor W. Adorno, Donald Gramm\n- Works: Lulu, Don Giovanni, Falstaff\n- Roles: Dr. Schön, Jack the Ripper, Leporello\n- Topics: opera, critical theory\n\nFacts:\n- Theodor W. Adorno was born as Theodor Ludwig Wiesengrund on September 11, 1903, and he became a German philosopher, sociologist, and composer known for critical theory of society.\n- Theodor W. Adorno wrote that the opera \"Lulu\" reveals more of its quality the longer and more deeply one immerses oneself in it.\n- Donald Gramm was notably known for performing the title role in Verdi's \"Falstaff,\" Leporello in Mozart's \"Don Giovanni,\" and Dr. Schön and Jack the Ripper in Berg's \"Lulu.\"\n- Theodor W. Adorno died on August 6, 1969.",
